From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - hash a long AES-XCBC digest in software on SPU-M

SPU-M cannot continue an AES-XCBC MAC across messages, so ahash_init(),
ahash_update() and ahash_finup() hash it in software when
spu_no_incr_hash() says so. ahash_digest() always goes to the hardware,
and handle_ahash_req() splits a digest longer than max_payload (65520
bytes for AES-XCBC) into several SPU messages. Each message starts a
new MAC under the original key, and the digest returned is the MAC of
the last chunk alone. On BCM6755, an AF_ALG digest through
xcbc-aes-iproc of 65521 or 65536 bytes gives the wrong MAC, while
65519 and 65520 bytes are correct.

Take the software path for a digest that does not fit in one message.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2339,10 +2339,21 @@ ahash_finup_exit:
 
 static int ahash_digest(struct ahash_request *req)
 {
+	struct crypto_ahash *tfm = crypto_ahash_reqtfm(req);
+	struct iproc_ctx_s *ctx = crypto_ahash_ctx(tfm);
 	int err;
 
 	flow_log("ahash_digest() nbytes:%u\n", req->nbytes);
 
+	if (spu_no_incr_hash(ctx) &&
+	    (ctx->max_payload != SPU_MAX_PAYLOAD_INF) &&
+	    (req->nbytes > ctx->max_payload)) {
+		err = ahash_init(req);
+		if (!err)
+			err = ahash_finup(req);
+		return err;
+	}
+
 	/* whole thing at once */
 	err = __ahash_init(req);
 	if (!err)
